WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.168 --> 00:00:19.225
Morb, the troll, and the entire room faded from view as Zann slid into the wormhole behind Wyssa.

2
00:00:19.226 --> 00:00:23.186
It was like nothing he'd ever seen or experienced before.

3
00:00:23.187 --> 00:00:29.686
It felt like falling—or flying. Zann found it difficult to breathe or think as he plummeted forward.

4
00:00:29.687 --> 00:00:36.460
Or was it downward? Or upward? He couldn't tell, and it made him feel dizzy and confused.

5
00:00:36.461 --> 00:00:40.123
He put out his free hand, trying to slow himself down.

6
00:00:40.124 --> 00:00:44.003
But there was nothing to grab, and his body twisted wildly.

7
00:00:44.004 --> 00:00:50.843
"Be careful!" Wyssa's voice echoed strangely. "Do not pull yourself off course!"

8
00:00:50.844 --> 00:00:56.011
Zann opened his mouth to answer but no words came out. He looked around.

9
00:00:56.012 --> 00:01:00.254
The wormhole was dark, filled with swirling shapes and colors.

10
00:01:00.255 --> 00:01:04.523
Every few seconds he and Wyssa slid past bright spots.

11
00:01:04.524 --> 00:01:09.137
Were those other wormholes? Did some of them lead to different worlds?

12
00:01:09.138 --> 00:01:12.129
Zann tried to focus on the next one they approached.

13
00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.227
He stared through it as they passed by, trying to catch a glimpse of what lay beyond.

14
00:01:17.228 --> 00:01:25.204
He saw a peaceful field of tall, amber grasses waving in the breeze with huge, strange-looking animals grazing.

15
00:01:25.205 --> 00:01:31.850
The sky above was a clear, pale purple; a pair of silver suns shone down on the scene.

16
00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:37.908
That was all Zann was able to take in before he was past the wormhole, but it was enough to set his mind spinning.

17
00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:42.586
It was amazing. How many different worlds were out there? What were they like?

18
00:01:42.587 --> 00:01:45.582
No wonder his parents had loved exploring so much!

19
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:52.060
When the next wormhole appeared, Zann reached out to grab its edge, hoping to slow down so he could get a good look.

20
00:01:52.061 --> 00:01:58.800
The movement sent him twisting sideways. This time he felt his hand start to slip from Wyssa's grip.

21
00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:04.521
"No!" Wyssa yelled harshly, grabbing him with both hands and yanking him forward.

22
00:02:04.522 --> 00:02:07.521
Zann glanced back longingly at the wormhole.

23
00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:09.850
He hadn't seen much more this time.

24
00:02:09.851 --> 00:02:15.405
Mostly swirling blue-green water with large, dark shapes drifting through it.

25
00:02:15.406 --> 00:02:18.530
Was it an ocean, perhaps one in Magica?

26
00:02:18.531 --> 00:02:23.335
Or could it be yet another faraway world full of wondrous creatures?

27
00:02:23.336 --> 00:02:27.803
Wyssa pulled him even with her; her eyes flashed angrily in the darkness.

28
00:02:27.804 --> 00:02:33.657
"I told you not to do that!" she scolded. "This is no place for amateurs.

29
00:02:33.658 --> 00:02:39.473
Do not try to stop or slow down again unless you wish to stay lost like your parents."

30
00:02:39.474 --> 00:02:45.789
Zann frowned, wanting to protest. But he was distracted by yet more wormholes flashing by.

31
00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:51.069
How could Wyssa just slide past them, ignoring the incredible scenes within?

32
00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:58.202
Then instead of rushing headlong, they were slowing down, though Zann couldn't tell how Wyssa had made that happen.

33
00:02:58.203 --> 00:03:00.721
They were approaching another bright spot.

34
00:03:00.722 --> 00:03:07.020
Wyssa reached out with her free hand, and before Zann realized what was happening, they were through the wormhole.

35
00:03:07.021 --> 00:03:11.114
"Oof," he grunted, landing facedown on the ground.

36
00:03:11.115 --> 00:03:16.270
Zann's head was reeling, and for a moment all he could do was lie there.

37
00:03:16.271 --> 00:03:22.752
Finally he pushed himself up and saw that they'd emerged beside the ancient tree in Wormwood.

38
00:03:22.753 --> 00:03:26.853
"Wow!" he said, once he'd caught his breath enough to speak.

39
00:03:26.854 --> 00:03:32.143
"That was amazing! How did you learn how to find wormholes like that?

40
00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:36.252
How did you know which one led here? How did you—"

41
00:03:36.253 --> 00:03:42.823
Wyssa cut him off with a frown. "You need to get out of town. Morb will be coming for you."

42
00:03:42.824 --> 00:03:48.308
Reaching into a knothole in the tree, she pulled out a large cloth bag and opened it.

43
00:03:48.309 --> 00:03:52.255
Taking out a small object, she pressed it into Zann's hand.

44
00:03:52.256 --> 00:03:59.859
"If you ever see your grandfather again," she added, a little more softly, "give this to him. Now go."

45
00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.655
Zann looked down to see what she'd given him.

46
00:04:02.656 --> 00:04:11.869
It was a smooth, oblong stone. Its surface was a blend of swirling colors that seemed to shift and change with every glint of the sun.

47
00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.183
"What is it?" he asked.

48
00:04:14.184 --> 00:04:22.511
Wyssa didn't answer. Zann glanced up just in time to see her disappear back into the wormhole, clutching her bag.

49
00:04:22.512 --> 00:04:25.299
A second later the wormhole disappeared too.

50
00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:31.865
"Wait!" Zann cried. That wormhole was the only way he could ever hope to find his parents.

51
00:04:31.866 --> 00:04:35.731
And the only person who could help him travel through it was gone.

52
00:04:35.732 --> 00:04:39.771
Zann could never go through the wormhole by himself. Or could he?

53
00:04:39.772 --> 00:04:44.214
"I could probably figure out how it works," he thought.

54
00:04:44.215 --> 00:04:49.368
After all, he'd been waiting for an opportunity like this for four years, and here it was.

55
00:04:49.369 --> 00:04:54.217
All he had to do was step in, and he could be reunited with his mom and dad.

56
00:04:54.218 --> 00:04:59.301
It was now or never. Zann walked over to the tree, and the wormhole opened up.

57
00:04:59.302 --> 00:05:05.162
He gazed into the whirling darkness, took a deep breath, and put the stone in his pocket.

58
00:05:05.163 --> 00:05:10.268
As he did so, he felt something else in there—the troll talisman.

59
00:05:10.269 --> 00:05:13.026
Zann took the talisman out and looked at it.

60
00:05:13.027 --> 00:05:21.006
Trolls . . . Morb . . . What good would it do to bring his parents back to a world where virtually everyone was a prisoner of Morb?

61
00:05:21.007 --> 00:05:26.066
Magica needed Zann, and right now that was more important than his own needs.

62
00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:29.341
People were counting on him—he couldn't let them down.

63
00:05:29.342 --> 00:05:33.397
Zann took a step back, and the wormhole disappeared once more.

64
00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:37.291
When Zann turned around, a message moth was fluttering toward him.

65
00:05:37.292 --> 00:05:39.941
He reached out and let it land on his finger.

66
00:05:39.942 --> 00:05:44.181
It was from Fala, telling him where to meet her and the others in the forest.

67
00:05:44.182 --> 00:05:48.388
Zann let the message moth go and put the talisman back in his pocket.

68
00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:57.827
He took one last look at the ancient tree and then set out toward the forest.
